dzn: Copy multisampled depth-stencil textures with a blit on Intel

Intel's Direct3D 12 drivers copy multisampled depth-stencil textures
wrongly with CopyTextureRegion. On a UHD 770 (32.0.101.7092) and an Iris
Plus 650 (31.0.101.2145) under WSL2, 18 dEQP-VK
copy_and_blit.*.depth_stencil_msaa_copy cases failed: the stencil of a
whole D24S8 copy read back as 0 from row 16 on, and a copy from one layer
of a 4-sample D24S8 or D32 array to another left the destination layer at
its clear value. The RTX 4080 of the same laptop passed them all.
Neither a NULL source box nor moving the destination through a read
layout before the copy changed anything.

Dozen already turns a partial copy of a multisampled or depth-stencil
texture into a per-sample blit (D3D12 copies those only as whole
subresources), and the partial cases passed on Intel. On Intel GPUs,
copy every multisampled depth-stencil texture with that blit.

diff --git a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
index 741f257..08e7517 100644
--- a/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/microsoft/vulkan/dzn_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -5351,6 +5351,18 @@ dzn_CmdCopyImage2(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
       }
    }
 
+   /* Intel's Direct3D 12 drivers copy multisampled depth-stencil textures
+    * wrongly with CopyTextureRegion: on a UHD 770 and an Iris Plus 650 under
+    * WSL2 the copied stencil of a D24S8 texture read back as 0 below its
+    * first rows, and a copy between layers of a multisampled depth array
+    * did not show up in the destination layer. The per-sample blit, which
+    * Dozen already uses for partial copies of such textures, copies them
+    * right.
+    */
+   if (pdev->desc.vendor_id == 0x8086 && src->vk.samples > 1 &&
+       ((src->desc.Flags | dst->desc.Flags) & D3D12_RESOURCE_FLAG_ALLOW_DEPTH_STENCIL))
+      use_blit = true;
+
    if (use_blit) {
       /* This copy -> blit lowering doesn't work if the vkCmdCopyImage[2]() is
        * is issued on a transfer queue, but we don't have any better option
